-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: PART 3, EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS, Division 3 (ss 18 to 22).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.  Target compiler: main (build 109).
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is a yes the Act gives; JUST FALSE is a no the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- s 18(5) and s 19(4) are regulation-making powers (machinery, inert, reason 2).

§ `Part 3 -- Division 3, Proceedings before a tribunal`

§§ `s 18 -- proceedings in private`

-- s 18(1): all proceedings before a tribunal are conducted in private, subject to (2) to (5).
-- src:1257 | 18.—(1) Subject to subsections (2), (3), (4) and (5), all proceedings
-- src:1258 | before a tribunal are to be conducted in private.
@ref s 18(1) (src:1257-1258)
GIVEN `the proceedings are before a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the proceedings before the tribunal are conducted in private` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are before a tribunal`
    -- (the exceptions in (2), (3) and (4) are permissions to be present, answered by those subsections; this answer does not net them out)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: "all proceedings before a tribunal"; other proceedings are not spoken to
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 18(2)(a): on its own initiative or on a party's application, in the manner prescribed, a tribunal may allow individuals to assist in resolving the claim amicably through mediation or conciliation.
-- src:1262 | (2) A tribunal may, on its own initiative or on the application of any
-- src:1263 | party to the proceedings, and in the manner prescribed by Rules of
-- src:1264 | Court made under section 33, do either or both of the following:
-- src:1266 | (a) allow one or more individuals to assist in resolving the
-- src:1267 | claim amicably through mediation or conciliation;
@ref s 18(2)(a) (src:1262-1267)
GIVEN `the allowance is made in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court made under section 33` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2)(a) the tribunal may allow individuals to assist in resolving the claim amicably` MEANS
    IF `the allowance is made in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court made under section 33` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court", which are not among the sources; and, where the manner is not met, the text is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 18(2)(b): ... allow individuals of skill and experience in the matter to sit with the tribunal and act as assessors.
-- src:1262 | (2) A tribunal may, on its own initiative or on the application of any
-- src:1263 | party to the proceedings, and in the manner prescribed by Rules of
-- src:1264 | Court made under section 33, do either or both of the following:
-- src:1266 | (a) allow one or more individuals to assist in resolving the
-- src:1267 | claim amicably through mediation or conciliation;
-- src:1269 | (b) allow one or more individuals of skill and experience in the
-- src:1270 | matter to which the proceedings relate to sit with the
-- src:1271 | tribunal and act as assessors.
@ref s 18(2)(b) (src:1262-1271)
GIVEN `the allowance is made in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court made under section 33` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual is of skill and experience in the matter to which the proceedings relate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2)(b) the tribunal may allow the individual to sit with the tribunal and act as an assessor` MEANS
    IF `the allowance is made in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court made under section 33` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the individual is of skill and experience in the matter to which the proceedings relate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the power is for "individuals of skill and experience in the matter" and "in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 18(3): a tribunal may permit an officer appointed under section 3(2) of the Employment Act 1968 to participate by giving evidence, producing a document, record or thing, or making submissions.
-- src:1273 | (3) A tribunal may permit an officer appointed under section 3(2) of
-- src:1274 | the Employment Act 1968 to participate in any proceedings before a
-- src:1275 | tribunal by doing one or more of the following:
-- src:1280 | (a) giving evidence in the proceedings;
-- src:1282 | (b) producing any document, record or thing that is relevant to
-- src:1283 | the proceedings;
-- src:1285 | (c) making submissions in the proceedings.
@ref s 18(3) (src:1273-1285)
GIVEN `the person is an officer appointed under section 3(2) of the Employment Act 1968` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the participation is giving evidence, producing a relevant document, record or thing, or making submissions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(3) the tribunal may permit the officer to participate in the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer appointed under section 3(2) of the Employment Act 1968` AND `the participation is giving evidence, producing a relevant document, record or thing, or making submissions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the permission names "an officer appointed under section 3(2) of the Employment Act 1968" and three kinds of participation
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 18(4): a tribunal may permit to observe the hearing (a) a prescribed individual, (b) an individual in a prescribed class, (c) any other individual the tribunal deems fit.
-- src:1289 | (4) A tribunal may permit one or more of the following to observe
-- src:1290 | the hearing of a claim:
-- src:1292 | (a) any prescribed individual;
-- src:1294 | (b) any individual belonging to a prescribed class of
-- src:1295 | individuals;
-- src:1297 | (c) any other individual that the tribunal deems fit.
@ref s 18(4) (src:1289-1297)
GIVEN `the individual is prescribed, or belongs to a prescribed class of individuals` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal deems the individual fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(4) the tribunal may permit the individual to observe the hearing of the claim` MEANS
    IF `the individual is prescribed, or belongs to a prescribed class of individuals` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the tribunal deems the individual fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the permission is for the three kinds of individual; whether an individual is prescribed is outside the sources
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 18(6): to avoid doubt, (1) does not prevent a tribunal from hearing 2 or more claims together if it is convenient and does not prejudice any party.
-- src:1303 | (6) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) does not prevent a tribunal from
-- src:1304 | hearing 2 or more claims together, if it appears to the tribunal that
-- src:1305 | doing so is convenient and does not prejudice any party to any of
-- src:1306 | those claims.
@ref s 18(6) (src:1303-1306)
GIVEN `the tribunal hears two or more claims together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the tribunal that doing so is convenient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the tribunal that doing so does not prejudice any party to any of those claims` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(6) subsection (1) does not prevent the tribunal from hearing the claims together` MEANS
    IF `the tribunal hears two or more claims together` AND `it appears to the tribunal that doing so is convenient` AND `it appears to the tribunal that doing so does not prejudice any party to any of those claims`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: an avoidance-of-doubt clause that settles only the case it names; it does not say that (1) prevents the tribunal from hearing claims together where the conditions fail (marginal reading (b))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 19 -- representation before a tribunal`

-- s 19(5): "body corporate" includes a limited liability partnership as defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005.
-- src:1347 | (5) In this section —
-- src:1349 | “body corporate” includes a limited liability partnership as
-- src:1350 | defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships
-- src:1351 | Act 2005;
@ref s 19(5) “body corporate” (src:1347-1351)
GIVEN `it is a limited liability partnership as defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(5) the entity is a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `it is a limited liability partnership as defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“body corporate” includes a limited liability partnership"; the text does not say what else is a body corporate
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 19(5): "officer", in relation to a body corporate, means a director, partner, member of the committee of management, chief executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer.
-- src:1353 | “officer”, in relation to a body corporate, means a director,
-- src:1354 | partner, member of the committee of management, chief
-- src:1355 | executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the
-- src:1356 | body corporate.
@ref s 19(5) “officer” (src:1353-1356)
GIVEN position IS A `Position in a body corporate`
      `the position is similar to those listed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `Director` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Member of the committee of management` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Chief executive` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Manager` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Another position` THEN
        IF `the position is similar to those listed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“officer”, in relation to a body corporate, means a director, partner, member of the committee of management, chief executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 19(1) to (3): who may represent a party before a tribunal.  Same shape as section 5 for a mediation.
-- src:1310 | 19.—(1) Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3), a party to
-- src:1311 | proceedings before a tribunal —
-- src:1313 | (a) must act in person;
-- src:1315 | (b) cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor; and
-- src:1317 | (c) cannot be represented by an agent, whether paid or
-- src:1318 | otherwise.
-- src:1320 | (2) A party other than an individual may be represented —
-- src:1322 | (a) if the party is the Government, by a public officer;
-- src:1324 | (b) if the party is a body corporate, by an officer, or a full‑time
-- src:1325 | employee, of the body corporate;
-- src:1327 | (c) if the party is a partnership, by a partner, or a full‑time
-- src:1328 | employee, of the partnership;
-- src:1333 | (d) if the party is an unincorporated association, by a member
-- src:1334 | of the governing body, or a full‑time employee, of the
-- src:1335 | unincorporated association; or
-- src:1337 | (e) by any other individual prescribed by regulations made
-- src:1338 | under section 34.
-- src:1340 | (3) A party who is an individual may be represented by any other
-- src:1341 | individual by regulations made under section 34.
-- src:1343 | (4) For the purposes of subsections (2)(e) and (3), the regulations
-- src:1344 | made under section 34 may prescribe different individuals for
-- src:1345 | different parties and different circumstances.
@ref s 19(1) to (4) (src:1310-1345)
GIVEN party IS A `Kind of party`
      representative IS A `Kind of representative`
      `the regulations prescribe the representative for the party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- (2)(a)
        IF party EQUALS `The Government` AND representative EQUALS `A public officer` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (2)(b)
        IF party EQUALS `A body corporate` AND (representative EQUALS `An officer of the body corporate` OR representative EQUALS `A full-time employee of the party`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (2)(c)
        IF party EQUALS `A partnership` AND (representative EQUALS `A partner of the partnership` OR representative EQUALS `A full-time employee of the party`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (2)(d)
        IF party EQUALS `An unincorporated association` AND (representative EQUALS `A member of the governing body of the unincorporated association` OR representative EQUALS `A full-time employee of the party`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (2)(e) and (3): an individual prescribed by regulations
        IF representative EQUALS `Another individual prescribed by regulations` AND `the regulations prescribe the representative for the party` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations prescribe this individual for this party is not among the sources
        IF representative EQUALS `Another individual prescribed by regulations` AND `the regulations prescribe the representative for the party` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor"
        IF representative EQUALS `An advocate and solicitor` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cannot be represented by an agent, whether paid or otherwise"
        IF representative EQUALS `An agent, whether paid or otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a party to proceedings before a tribunal (a) must act in person" -- any other representative is outside (2) and (3)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 19(1)(b) and (c) as regulative rules: a party SHANT be represented by an advocate and solicitor, or by an agent, except as (2) and (3) allow.
-- src:1310 | 19.—(1) Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3), a party to
-- src:1311 | proceedings before a tribunal —
-- src:1313 | (a) must act in person;
-- src:1315 | (b) cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor; and
@ref s 19(1)(b) (src:1310-1315)
GIVEN party IS AN `Actor under the Act`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 19(1)(b) the party's prohibition on representation by an advocate and solicitor` MEANS
    PARTY party
    SHANT `be represented by an advocate and solicitor`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "a party to proceedings before a tribunal was represented by an advocate and solicitor"

-- src:1310 | 19.—(1) Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3), a party to
-- src:1311 | proceedings before a tribunal —
-- src:1313 | (a) must act in person;
-- src:1315 | (b) cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor; and
-- src:1317 | (c) cannot be represented by an agent, whether paid or
-- src:1318 | otherwise.
@ref s 19(1)(c) (src:1310-1318)
GIVEN party IS AN `Actor under the Act`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 19(1)(c) the party's prohibition on representation by an agent` MEANS
    PARTY party
    SHANT `be represented by an agent`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "a party to proceedings before a tribunal was represented by an agent"

