§§ `s 21 -- evidence`

-- s 21(1)(a): a tribunal is not bound by the rules of evidence in the conduct of any proceedings.
-- src:1420 | 21.—(1) A tribunal —
-- src:1422 | (a) is not bound by the rules of evidence in the conduct of any
-- src:1423 | proceedings; and
@ref s 21(1)(a) (src:1420-1423)
`s 21(1)(a) the tribunal is not bound by the rules of evidence` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 21(1)(b): a tribunal may inform itself on any matter in any manner that it thinks fit.
-- src:1420 | 21.—(1) A tribunal —
-- src:1422 | (a) is not bound by the rules of evidence in the conduct of any
-- src:1423 | proceedings; and
-- src:1425 | (b) may inform itself on any matter in any manner that the
-- src:1426 | tribunal thinks fit.
@ref s 21(1)(b) (src:1420-1426)
`s 21(1)(b) the tribunal may inform itself on any matter in any manner it thinks fit` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 21(2): a tribunal may draw any inferences it thinks fit from a party's failure to comply with an obligation under a written law specified in the Fourth Schedule, including an inference that unavailable evidence would, if produced, have been unfavourable to that party.
-- src:1431 | (2) A tribunal may draw any inferences that the tribunal thinks fit
-- src:1432 | from a party’s failure to comply with any obligation of that party
-- src:1433 | under any written law specified in the Fourth Schedule, including
-- src:1434 | (but not limited to) an inference that any evidence that is not available
-- src:1435 | on account of that party’s failure to comply with that obligation
-- src:1436 | would, if produced, have been unfavourable to that party.
@ref s 21(2) (src:1431-1436)
GIVEN obligation IS AN `Obligation of a party under a written law`
      `the party failed to comply with that obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(2) the tribunal may draw any inference it thinks fit from the party's failure` MEANS
    CONSIDER obligation
    WHEN `A Fourth Schedule obligation` item THEN
        IF `the party failed to comply with that obligation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the power arises from "failure to comply with any obligation of that party under any written law specified in the Fourth Schedule"; the clause names what the inference is drawn from and carries no "only"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the power is for obligations under a written law specified in the Fourth Schedule
    WHEN `Some other obligation` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1431 | (2) A tribunal may draw any inferences that the tribunal thinks fit
-- src:1432 | from a party’s failure to comply with any obligation of that party
-- src:1433 | under any written law specified in the Fourth Schedule, including
-- src:1434 | (but not limited to) an inference that any evidence that is not available
-- src:1435 | on account of that party’s failure to comply with that obligation
-- src:1436 | would, if produced, have been unfavourable to that party.
@ref s 21(2) (src:1431-1436)
GIVEN obligation IS AN `Obligation of a party under a written law`
      `the party failed to comply with that obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(2) the inference may include that unavailable evidence would, if produced, have been unfavourable to the party` MEANS
    `s 21(2) the tribunal may draw any inference it thinks fit from the party's failure` obligation `the party failed to comply with that obligation`

-- s 21(3): subject to (4), evidence tendered to a tribunal need not be given on oath or affirmation.
-- src:1440 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), evidence tendered to a tribunal need
-- src:1441 | not be given on oath or affirmation.
@ref s 21(3) (src:1440-1441)
GIVEN `the tribunal requires the evidence to be given on oath or affirmation under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3) the evidence need not be given on oath or affirmation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the tribunal requires the evidence to be given on oath or affirmation under subsection (4)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (4), evidence tendered to a tribunal need not be given on oath or affirmation" (the tribunal requires it under (4))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 21(4)(a): a tribunal may require the whole or any part of any evidence, oral or written, to be given on oath or affirmation.
-- src:1443 | (4) A tribunal may —
-- src:1445 | (a) require the whole or any part of any evidence tendered to a
-- src:1446 | tribunal, whether orally or in writing, to be given on oath or
-- src:1447 | affirmation; and
@ref s 21(4)(a) (src:1443-1447)
`s 21(4)(a) the tribunal may require evidence to be given on oath or affirmation` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 21(4)(b): and may for that purpose administer an oath or affirmation.
-- src:1443 | (4) A tribunal may —
-- src:1445 | (a) require the whole or any part of any evidence tendered to a
-- src:1446 | tribunal, whether orally or in writing, to be given on oath or
-- src:1447 | affirmation; and
-- src:1449 | (b) for that purpose, administer an oath or affirmation.
@ref s 21(4)(b) (src:1443-1449)
`s 21(4)(b) the tribunal may administer an oath or affirmation for that purpose` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 21(5): a tribunal may on its own initiative seek other evidence and make other investigations and inquiries as it thinks fit.
-- src:1451 | (5) A tribunal may, on its own initiative, seek such other evidence,
-- src:1452 | and make such other investigations and inquiries, as the tribunal
-- src:1453 | thinks fit.
@ref s 21(5) (src:1451-1453)
`s 21(5) the tribunal may seek other evidence and make other investigations and inquiries on its own initiative` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 21(6): all evidence and information the tribunal obtained under (5) must be disclosed to every party.
-- src:1455 | (6) All evidence and information obtained by a tribunal under
-- src:1456 | subsection (5) for any proceedings must be disclosed to every party to
-- src:1457 | those proceedings.
@ref s 21(6) (src:1455-1457)
GIVEN `the evidence or information was obtained by the tribunal under subsection (5) for the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6) the evidence and information must be disclosed to every party to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the evidence or information was obtained by the tribunal under subsection (5) for the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the duty is for "evidence and information obtained by a tribunal under subsection (5)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 21(6) as a regulative rule: the tribunal MUST disclose.  The Act sets no time, so no WITHIN.
-- src:1455 | (6) All evidence and information obtained by a tribunal under
-- src:1456 | subsection (5) for any proceedings must be disclosed to every party to
-- src:1457 | those proceedings.
@ref s 21(6) (src:1455-1457)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in the proceedings` `Act in the proceedings`
`s 21(6) the tribunal's duty to disclose the evidence it obtained` MEANS
    PARTY `The tribunal`
    MUST `disclose to every party the evidence and information obtained under section 21(5)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The tribunal` BECAUSE "evidence or information obtained by the tribunal was not disclosed to every party"

-- s 21(7): a tribunal may require any written evidence to be verified by statutory declaration.
-- src:1459 | (7) A tribunal may require any written evidence given in
-- src:1460 | proceedings before a tribunal to be verified by statutory declaration.
@ref s 21(7) (src:1459-1460)
`s 21(7) the tribunal may require written evidence to be verified by statutory declaration` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 21(8): a tribunal need not keep a record of the evidence given, but must make (a) a summary of the facts and issues in dispute, as determined by the tribunal; and (b) notes of the proceedings.
-- src:1462 | (8) A tribunal need not keep a record of the evidence given in any
