@ref s 21(8)(a) (src:1462-1466)
GIVEN `the tribunal conducts proceedings on a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(8)(a) the tribunal must make a summary of the facts and issues in dispute` MEANS
    IF `the tribunal conducts proceedings on a claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the duty is for "any proceedings before the tribunal"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1462 | (8) A tribunal need not keep a record of the evidence given in any
-- src:1463 | proceedings before the tribunal, but must make —
-- src:1465 | (a) a summary of the facts and issues in dispute, as determined
