-- src:1468 | (b) notes of the proceedings.
@ref s 21(8)(b) (src:1462-1468)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in the proceedings` `Act in the proceedings`
`s 21(8)(b) the tribunal's duty to make notes of the proceedings` MEANS
    PARTY `The tribunal`
    MUST `make notes of the proceedings`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The tribunal` BECAUSE "no notes of the proceedings were made"

§§ `s 22 -- orders of a tribunal`

-- s 22(1): a tribunal may determine a claim within its jurisdiction by making one or more of four kinds of order.
-- src:1471 | 22.—(1) A tribunal may determine a claim within the tribunal’s
-- src:1473 | jurisdiction by making one or more of the following orders:
-- src:1474 | (a) an order requiring a party to pay money to another party;
-- src:1475 | (b) an order dismissing the whole or any part of the claim;
-- src:1480 | (c) an order requiring a party to pay costs to another party;
-- src:1482 | (d) an order requiring an employer to reinstate an employee in
-- src:1483 | the employee’s former employment.
@ref s 22(1) (src:1471-1483)
GIVEN `the claim is within the tribunal's jurisdiction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      order IS AN `Order of a tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the power is "to determine a claim within the tribunal's jurisdiction"; a claim outside it is dealt with by section 22(7)
        IF NOT (`the claim is within the tribunal's jurisdiction` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "one or more of the following orders" does not say that no other kind of order may be made
        IF order EQUALS `Another kind of order` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 22(2): in deciding whether to make a costs order, a tribunal may take into account (a) a frivolous or vexatious claim; (b) a party's failure without reasonable excuse to attend a mediation of a dispute for which the claim is lodged; (c) a party's failure without reasonable excuse to attend proceedings it was required to attend.
-- src:1487 | (2) In deciding whether to make an order under subsection (1)(c), a
-- src:1488 | tribunal may take into account any of the following matters:
-- src:1490 | (a) whether the claim was frivolous or vexatious;
-- src:1492 | (b) whether a party without reasonable excuse failed to attend
-- src:1493 | a mediation under Part 2, or a tripartite mediation
-- src:1494 | (conducted by an approved mediator), of a specified
-- src:1495 | employment dispute for which the claim is lodged;
-- src:1497 | (c) whether any party without reasonable excuse failed to
-- src:1498 | attend any proceedings before the tribunal which that party
-- src:1499 | was required to attend.
@ref s 22(2) (src:1487-1499)
GIVEN `the claim was frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party without reasonable excuse failed to attend a mediation under Part 2, or a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator, of a specified employment dispute for which the claim is lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party without reasonable excuse failed to attend proceedings before the tribunal which that party was required to attend` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) the tribunal may take the matter into account in deciding whether to make a costs order` MEANS
    IF `the claim was frivolous or vexatious` OR `a party without reasonable excuse failed to attend a mediation under Part 2, or a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator, of a specified employment dispute for which the claim is lodged` OR `a party without reasonable excuse failed to attend proceedings before the tribunal which that party was required to attend`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may take into account any of the following matters" does not say that no other matter may be taken into account (section 33(2)(r) allows Rules of Court to add circumstances)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 22(3): a tribunal's order is subject to any conditions the tribunal thinks fit to impose.
-- src:1501 | (3) A tribunal’s order under subsection (1) is subject to any
-- src:1502 | conditions that the tribunal thinks fit to impose.
@ref s 22(3) (src:1501-1502)
`s 22(3) the order is subject to any conditions the tribunal thinks fit to impose` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 22(4): the total ordered to be paid to a party under (1)(a) for specified contractual and statutory disputes must not exceed the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) applicable to the party.
-- src:1504 | (4) The total amount of money that a tribunal orders to be paid to a
-- src:1505 | party under subsection (1)(a), in respect of every specified
-- src:1506 | contractual dispute (if any) and every specified statutory dispute (if
-- src:1507 | any) for which a claim is lodged, must not exceed the prescribed
-- src:1508 | claim limit in section 12(7)(a) that is applicable to the party.
@ref s 22(4) (src:1504-1508)
GIVEN `the total amount ordered to be paid to the party under subsection (1)(a) for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) applicable to the party` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(4) the total ordered to be paid for contractual and statutory disputes is within the claim limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) applicable to the party`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        -- (the text says "(if any)": a total of nothing cannot exceed a limit, whatever the limit is; fork F11)
        IF `the total amount ordered to be paid to the party under subsection (1)(a) for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute` AT MOST 0
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the prescribed claim limit" is set under section 12(8)(e) by regulations that are not among the sources
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN JUST limit THEN
        IF `the total amount ordered to be paid to the party under subsection (1)(a) for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute` AT MOST limit
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not exceed the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) that is applicable to the party"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 22(5): the same for wrongful dismissal disputes against the limit in section 12(7)(b).
-- src:1512 | (5) The total amount of money that a tribunal orders to be paid to a
-- src:1513 | party under subsection (1)(a), in respect of every wrongful dismissal
-- src:1514 | dispute (if any) for which a claim is lodged, must not exceed the
-- src:1515 | prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) that is applicable to the
-- src:1516 | party.
@ref s 22(5) (src:1512-1516)
GIVEN `the total amount ordered to be paid to the party under subsection (1)(a) for every wrongful dismissal dispute` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) applicable to the party` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(5) the total ordered to be paid for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the claim limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) applicable to the party`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        -- (the text says "(if any)": a total of nothing cannot exceed a limit, whatever the limit is; fork F11)
        IF `the total amount ordered to be paid to the party under subsection (1)(a) for every wrongful dismissal dispute` AT MOST 0
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the prescribed claim limit" is set under section 12(8)(e) by regulations that are not among the sources
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN JUST limit THEN
        IF `the total amount ordered to be paid to the party under subsection (1)(a) for every wrongful dismissal dispute` AT MOST limit
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not exceed the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) that is applicable to the party"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 22(6)(a): any amount ordered under (1)(a) does not include any costs ordered under (1)(c).  So of a total the tribunal orders a party to pay, costs included, the amount under (1)(a) is the total less the costs, and only that amount counts against the claim limits in (4) and (5).
-- src:1520 | (6) To avoid doubt —
-- src:1522 | (a) any amount of money that a tribunal orders to be paid
-- src:1523 | under subsection (1)(a) does not include any costs that a
-- src:1524 | tribunal orders to be paid under subsection (1)(c); and
@ref s 22(6)(a) (src:1520-1524)
GIVEN `the total sum the tribunal orders the party to pay, costs included` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs ordered to be paid under subsection (1)(c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(6)(a) the amount of money ordered under subsection (1)(a), which does not include costs` MEANS
    `the total sum the tribunal orders the party to pay, costs included` MINUS `the costs ordered to be paid under subsection (1)(c)`

-- s 22(6)(b): where both an amount and costs are ordered, money paid is applied first to the amount under (1)(a), and then to the costs under (1)(c).
-- src:1526 | (b) where a tribunal orders a party to pay an amount of money
-- src:1527 | under subsection (1)(a) and costs under subsection (1)(c),
-- src:1528 | any money paid by the party is to be applied first to the
-- src:1533 | payment of the amount under subsection (1)(a), and then to
-- src:1534 | the payment of the costs under subsection (1)(c).
@ref s 22(6)(b) (src:1526-1534)
GIVEN `the money the party has paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount ordered under subsection (1)(a)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the amount under subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the money the party has paid` AT MOST `the amount ordered under subsection (1)(a)`
    THEN `the money the party has paid`
    ELSE `the amount ordered under subsection (1)(a)`

-- src:1526 | (b) where a tribunal orders a party to pay an amount of money
-- src:1527 | under subsection (1)(a) and costs under subsection (1)(c),
-- src:1528 | any money paid by the party is to be applied first to the
-- src:1533 | payment of the amount under subsection (1)(a), and then to
-- src:1534 | the payment of the costs under subsection (1)(c).
@ref s 22(6)(b) (src:1526-1534)
GIVEN `the money the party has paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount ordered under subsection (1)(a)` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs ordered under subsection (1)(c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the costs under subsection (1)(c)` MEANS
    IF `the money the party has paid` AT MOST `the amount ordered under subsection (1)(a)`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the money the party has paid` MINUS `the amount ordered under subsection (1)(a)` AT MOST `the costs ordered under subsection (1)(c)`
         THEN `the money the party has paid` MINUS `the amount ordered under subsection (1)(a)`
         ELSE `the costs ordered under subsection (1)(c)`

-- s 22(7): where a tribunal does not have jurisdiction to determine a claim or a part of it, that claim or part must be dismissed for lack of jurisdiction.
-- src:1536 | (7) Where a tribunal does not have jurisdiction to determine a claim
-- src:1537 | or any part of a claim, that claim or part (as the case may be) must be
-- src:1538 | dismissed for lack of jurisdiction.
@ref s 22(7) (src:1536-1538)
GIVEN `the tribunal does not have jurisdiction to determine the claim or the part of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(7) the claim or the part must be dismissed for lack of jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the tribunal does not have jurisdiction to determine the claim or the part of the claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a tribunal does not have jurisdiction to determine a claim or a part of it" [ruled (b)] (it has jurisdiction)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 22(8): instead of determining a claim by an order, a tribunal may refer any specified employment dispute for mediation under Part 2 (if the claim arose from a Part 2 mediation) or for tripartite mediation by an approved mediator (if it arose from one), with or without the parties' consent.
-- src:1540 | (8) A tribunal may, instead of determining a claim by making an
-- src:1541 | order under subsection (1), refer any specified employment dispute
-- src:1542 | for which the claim is lodged for mediation under Part 2 (if the claim
-- src:1543 | arose from a mediation under Part 2) or for tripartite mediation to be
-- src:1544 | conducted by an approved mediator (if the claim arose from a
-- src:1545 | tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator), with or
-- src:1546 | without the consent of the parties.
@ref s 22(8) (src:1540-1546)
GIVEN origin IS A `Where a claim arose`
      `the parties to the specified employment dispute consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of mediation referred to`
`s 22(8) the kind of mediation the tribunal may refer the dispute to` MEANS
    CONSIDER origin
    WHEN `From a mediation under Part 2 of a specified employment dispute` THEN JUST `Mediation under Part 2`
    WHEN `From a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator` THEN JUST `Tripartite mediation to be conducted by an approved mediator`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [no yes-or-no]: the power is for a claim that "arose from a mediation under Part 2" or "from a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator"; the function returns a kind of mediation, so there is no JUST FALSE to give
    WHEN `From neither of those` THEN NOTHING

-- s 22(9): when making a referral under (8), a tribunal may order all or any of the parties to attend the mediation personally.
-- src:1548 | (9) A tribunal may, when making a referral under subsection (8),
-- src:1549 | order all or any of the parties to personally attend the mediation under
-- src:1550 | Part 2 or the tripartite mediation (as the case may be).
@ref s 22(9) (src:1548-1550)
GIVEN `the tribunal is making a referral under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(9) the tribunal may order the parties to attend the mediation personally` MEANS
    IF `the tribunal is making a referral under subsection (8)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when making a referral under subsection (8)" [assumed: when] (the tribunal is not making one)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 22(10): the tribunal may correct an order within 14 days after the date it is made, or a statement of grounds within 14 days after the date it is issued, to the extent necessary to rectify (a) a clerical mistake, (b) an error arising from an accidental slip or omission, (c) a material miscalculation of figures or mistake in the description of a person, thing or matter, (d) a defect of form.
-- src:1552 | (10) A tribunal may correct an order made by the tribunal within
-- src:1553 | 14 days after the date on which the order is made, or correct a
-- src:1554 | statement of the tribunal’s grounds for making the order within
-- src:1555 | 14 days after the date on which the statement is issued by the tribunal,
-- src:1556 | to the extent necessary to rectify any of the following things:
@ref s 22(10) (src:1552-1556)
GIVEN `the date on which the order is made, or the statement of grounds is issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 22(10) the last day on which the tribunal may make the correction` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL ((DATE_SERIAL `the date on which the order is made, or the statement of grounds is issued`) PLUS 14)

-- src:1552 | (10) A tribunal may correct an order made by the tribunal within
-- src:1553 | 14 days after the date on which the order is made, or correct a
-- src:1554 | statement of the tribunal’s grounds for making the order within
-- src:1555 | 14 days after the date on which the statement is issued by the tribunal,
-- src:1556 | to the extent necessary to rectify any of the following things:
-- src:1558 | (a) a clerical mistake;
-- src:1560 | (b) an error arising from an accidental slip or omission;
-- src:1562 | (c) a material miscalculation of figures, or a material mistake
-- src:1563 | in the description of any person, thing or matter, referred to
-- src:1564 | in the order or statement (as the case may be);
-- src:1566 | (d) a defect of form.
@ref s 22(10) (src:1552-1566)
GIVEN `the date on which the order is made, or the statement of grounds is issued` IS A DATE
      `the date of the correction` IS A DATE
      `the correction rectifies a clerical mistake, an error arising from an accidental slip or omission, a material miscalculation or mistake in a description, or a defect of form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date on which the order is made" [ruled (a)] (the correction is later; a District Court may extend the time under section 23(3)(a), and that extension is not an input of this function)
        IF `the date of the correction` GREATER THAN `s 22(10) the last day on which the tribunal may make the correction` `the date on which the order is made, or the statement of grounds is issued` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the correction rectifies a clerical mistake, an error arising from an accidental slip or omission, a material miscalculation or mistake in a description, or a defect of form` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: the power is "to the extent necessary to rectify" the four things, and a correction that changes the merits is outside that extent; the clause carries no "only"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 22(10) as a regulative rule: the tribunal MAY correct WITHIN 14 days.
-- src:1552 | (10) A tribunal may correct an order made by the tribunal within
-- src:1553 | 14 days after the date on which the order is made, or correct a
-- src:1554 | statement of the tribunal’s grounds for making the order within
-- src:1555 | 14 days after the date on which the statement is issued by the tribunal,
-- src:1556 | to the extent necessary to rectify any of the following things:
@ref s 22(10) (src:1552-1556)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in the proceedings` `Act in the proceedings`
`s 22(10) the tribunal's permission to correct an order within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `The tribunal`
    MAY `correct an order made by the tribunal`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- s 22(11): the tribunal may make the correction on its own initiative or on a party's application.
-- src:1568 | (11) The tribunal may make the correction in subsection (10) on its
-- src:1569 | own initiative or on the application of a party to the proceedings
-- src:1570 | before the tribunal.
@ref s 22(11) (src:1568-1570)
`s 22(11) the tribunal may make the correction on its own initiative or on the application of a party` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 22(12): every order made by a tribunal under (1) may be enforced in the same manner as a judgment or order of a District Court.
-- src:1572 | (12) Every order made by a tribunal under subsection (1) may be
-- src:1573 | enforced in the same manner as a judgment given or an order made by
-- src:1574 | a District Court.
@ref s 22(12) (src:1572-1574)
GIVEN `the order was made by a tribunal under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(12) the order may be enforced in the same manner as a judgment given or an order made by a District Court` MEANS
    IF `the order was made by a tribunal under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: "Every order made by a tribunal under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING
